{"id":1749824,"retrievedAt":"2026-08-15T11:41:28.918Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/Ahog8zVi1oXZhdtgNzC2iMXsbas.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":27,"name":"Horror"}],"homepage":"","id":1749824,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"LUTAO","overview":"LUTAO is an independent Filipino folk horror short film by INATO Pictures, written and directed by Michael Enolpe Compoc from a story concept with Harsey Panisa Antocan. Set in a remote Mindanao Muslim village, the 20-minute film blends the regional folklore of the Lutao with the Southeast Asian Pocong legend, a shroud-wrapped corpse returning from the grave.  ​Rather than a simple retelling, LUTAO crafts an original apocalyptic survival thriller. The horror begins when a fisherman unearths a hidden forest grave, unleashing an unexplainable outbreak upon the quiet community. As chaos spreads, one family fights to survive while confronting fear, faith, buried secrets, and grief.  ​Told through authentic Bisaya and Tausug storytelling, LUTAO explores themes of accountability and compassion. Created entirely without a production budget or sponsors, this passion project celebrates Mindanaoan cultural identity while offering a bold, fresh vision for local and international audiences.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/pp8NCNpbZQIUVXx9RbvVHzLvc96.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":307608,"logo_path":null,"name":"INATO Pictures","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"PH","name":"Philippines"}],"release_date":"2026-11-01","revenue":0,"runtime":21,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"Not every corpse is meant to rest.","title":"LUTAO","video":true,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6412746,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"RENNIELLE GOLOSINO","original_name":"RENNIELLE GOLOSINO","popularity":0,"profile_path